      ":question/id": "af56a79c-d704-5a7b-bb90-6dd90345820d",
      ":question/problem": "A tutoring center currently has $10$ enrolled students. The number of students in the center $T(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. If the maximum capacity of the tutoring center is $95$ students, which differential equation could be used to model the student population of the center? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
